{\plain \fs36 \i\f3\fs36 Concerning the Service}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 This Order provides a form of evening service or vespers for use on\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 suitable occasions in the late afternoon or evening.  It may be used as a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 complete rite in place of Evening Prayer, or as the introduction to\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Evening Prayer or some other service, or as the prelude to an evening\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 meal or other activity.  It is appropriate also for use in private \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 houses.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Any part or parts of this service may be led by lay persons.  A priest or\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 deacon, when presiding, should read the Prayer for Light, and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Blessing or Dismissal at the end.  The bishop, when present, should give\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 the Blessing. \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 This order is not appropriate for use on Monday, Tuesday, or Wednesday\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 in Holy Week, or on Good Friday.  Easter Eve has its own form for the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Lighting of the Paschal Candle. \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 For the Short Lesson at the beginning of the service, any one of the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 following is also appropriate, especially for the seasons suggested:\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Isaiah 60:19-20 (Advent)\ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab Revelation 21:10,22-24 (Easter)}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Luke 12:35-37 (Advent)\ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab Psalm 36:5-9 (Ascension)}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 John 1:1-5 (Christmas)\ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab Joel 2:28-30 (Whitsunday)}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Isaiah 60:1-3 (Epiphany)\ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab Colossians 1:9,11-14 (Saints' Days)}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 1 John 1:5-7 (Lent)\ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab 1 Peter 2:9 (Saints' Days)}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\fi-2880\li2880\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 John 12:35-36 A (Lent) \ul0 \tab \ul0 \tab Revelation 22:1,4-5 (Saints' Days) }{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
