}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 may follow the Psalmody.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \b\f3\fs20 Bible Reading}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 .  A sermon or homily, a passage from Christian literature,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 or a brief silence, may follow the Reading.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \b\f3\fs20 Canticle.}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20   The Magnificat or other canticle, or some other hymn of praise.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \b\f3\fs20 Prayers.}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20   A litany, or other suitable devotions, including the Lord's Prayer.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \b\f3\fs20 Blessing or Dismissal,}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  or both.  The Peace may then be exchanged. \par
