}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 On feasts or other days of special significance, the Collect of the \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Day, or one proper to the season, may precede the Blessing or Dismissal.  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 On other days, either of the following, or one of the Collects from \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Evening Prayer or from Compline, may be so used.}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Blessed are you, O Lord, the God of our fathers, creator\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 of the changes of day and night, giving rest to the weary,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 renewing the strength of those who are spent, bestowing\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 upon us occasions of song in the evening.  As you have\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 protected us in the day that is past, so be with us in the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 coming night; keep us from every sin, every evil, and every\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 fear; for you are our light and salvation, and the strength of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 our life. To you be glory for endless ages.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Almighty, everlasting God, let our prayer in your sight be as\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 incense, the lifting up of our hands as the evening sacrifice.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Give us grace to behold you, present in your Word and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Sacraments, and to recognize you in the lives of those around\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 us.  Stir up in us the flame of that love which burned in the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 heart of your Son as he bore his passion, and let it burn in us\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 to eternal life and to the ages of ages.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
